<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:32:default:windows">
<!--
    pebnames, the x86 twin of kuna-pebnames.xml: on x86 the TEB is at the FS base,
    the PEB pointer is TEB+0x30, TEB.Self is +0x18, and NtGlobalFlag is PEB+0x68.

    Layout (x86 Windows):
      0x401000  64 a1 30 00 00 00                     mov eax,fs:[0x30]   ; TEB.ProcessEnvironmentBlock
      0x401006  0f b6 48 02 / 85 c9 / 75 1b           movzx ecx,byte [eax+2] ; test ; jne dbg
      0x40100e  8b 48 68 / 83 e1 70 / 83 f9 70 / 74 10  mov ecx,[eax+0x68] ; and ; cmp ; je dbg
      0x401019  64 a1 18 00 00 00                     mov eax,fs:[0x18]   ; TEB.Self
      0x40101f  8b 40 30 / 8b 40 18 / 8b 40 40 / c3   ->PEB ; ->ProcessHeap ; heap+0x40 ; ret
      0x401029  b8 01 00 00 00 / c3                   dbg: mov eax,1 ; ret

    Pass 1 (pebnames off, the bug): the FS base is an untyped register and every
    read is a magic offset.
    Pass 2 (pebnames on, the fix): TEB *teb // fs_offset, and the probes read by name.

    A function that writes through the base is left untyped. Every x86 function
    with an exception handler links a registration record into TEB.ExceptionList
    and unlinks it on exit, and the record's stack layout is inferred from how the
    untyped base is used, so typing the base would rearrange that frame:
      0x401040  55 / 89 e5 / 6a ff / 68 00 12 40 00   push ebp ; mov ebp,esp ; push -1 ; push handler
      0x40104a  64 a1 00 00 00 00 / 50                mov eax,fs:[0] ; push eax
      0x401051  64 89 25 00 00 00 00                  mov fs:[0],esp      ; link the record
      0x401058  64 a1 30 00 00 00 / 0f b6 40 02       mov eax,fs:[0x30] ; movzx eax,byte [eax+2]
      0x401062  8b 4d f4 / 64 89 0d 00 00 00 00       mov ecx,[ebp-0xc] ; mov fs:[0],ecx
      0x40106c  89 ec / 5d / c3                       mov esp,ebp ; pop ebp ; ret
    Passes 3 and 4 decompile it off and on, and the two renders must agree: the
    12-byte record stays one object and the PEB read stays an array element of
    the base. Passes 5 and 6 do the same for MSVC's C++ EH prologue, whose
    record {Next, handler, state} is linked through a pointer taken after the
    /GS cookie push; typing the base there split the record into three unrelated
    scalars:
      0x401080  6a ff / 68 00 13 40 00 / 64 a1 00 00 00 00 / 50   push -1 ; push handler ; push fs:[0]
      0x40108e  51 / 56 / a1 10 20 40 00 / 31 e0 / 50            push ecx ; push esi ; cookie ^ esp
      0x401098  8d 44 24 0c / 64 a3 00 00 00 00                  lea eax,[esp+0xc] ; mov fs:[0],eax
      0x4010a2  ... call 0x401400 ...                             body
      0x4010be  8b 4c 24 0c / 64 89 0d 00 00 00 00               mov ecx,[esp+0xc] ; mov fs:[0],ecx

    Near misses, decompiled under pebnames on, none of which may gain a name:
      0x401100  mov eax,fs:[0x1010]       ; inside the Windows 11 WOW64 TEB32 (0x1038 bytes)
      0x401110  mov eax,fs:[0x1040]       ; 0x1038 + 8: past the largest TEB32, lined up
                                          ; with StackLimit
      0x401120  mov ecx,fs:[0x30]
                movzx eax,byte [ecx+3]    ; SpareBool on XP, BitField after it
                add eax,[ecx+0x38]        ; ApiSetMap from Windows 7, FreeList before it
      0x401130  mov eax,fs:[0x30]
                mov eax,[eax+0x490]       ; 0x488 + 8: past the largest PEB32, lined up
                                          ; with ImageBaseAddress
      0x401140  mov eax,gs:[0x14]         ; GS is not the TEB on x86
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x401000" readonly="true"></bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x401000" name="anti_debug32"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x401040" name="seh_frame32"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x401080" name="eh_frame32"/>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x401100" readonly="true">64a110100000c3cccccccccccccccccc64a140100000c3cccccccccccccccccc648b0d300000000fb64103034138c3cc64a1300000008b8090040000c3cccccc65a114000000c3cccccccccccccccccc</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x401100" name="hole_1010"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x401110" name="past_end32"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x401120" name="version_holes32"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x401130" name="peb_past_end32"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x401140" name="gs_32"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option pebnames off</com>
  <com>lo fu anti_debug32</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option pebnames on</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option pebnames off</com>
  <com>lo fu seh_frame32</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option pebnames on</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option pebnames off</com>
  <com>lo fu eh_frame32</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option pebnames on</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu hole_1010</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu past_end32</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu version_holes32</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu peb_past_end32</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu gs_32</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="PEBNAMES-X86 #1: BeingDebugged is read through FS:[0x30] by name (on pass only)" min="1" max="1">\(!teb-&gt;ProcessEnvironmentBlock-&gt;BeingDebugged\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="PEBNAMES-X86 #2: NtGlobalFlag sits at PEB+0x68 on x86 (on pass only)" min="1" max="1">\(teb-&gt;ProcessEnvironmentBlock-&gt;NtGlobalFlag &amp; 0x70\) != 0x70</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="PEBNAMES-X86 #3: FS:[0x18] is TEB.Self and chains on to the ProcessHeap (on pass only)" min="1" max="1">teb-&gt;Self-&gt;ProcessEnvironmentBlock-&gt;ProcessHeap \+ 0x40</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="PEBNAMES-X86 #4: the magic-offset read of BeingDebugged (off pass only)" min="1" max="1">!\*\(char \*\)\(\*\(int4 \*\)\(v[0-9]+ \+ 0x30\) \+ 2\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="PEBNAMES-X86 #5: the TEB pointer is declared for the reader and every near miss, never for the function that writes the base" min="5" max="5">TEB \*teb; // fs_offset</stringmatch>
